"Simply supported beam
'Length -'L = 6m
'Load -'q = 10kN/m
'Shear -'V_0 = q*L/2
'Bending -'M_max = q*L^2/8
'Diagrams
V(x) = V_0 - q*x
M(x) = V_0*x - q*x^2/2
PlotHeight = 100
$Plot{V(x) @ x = 0m : L}
$Plot{M(x) @ x = 0m : L}

"Axial resistance of steel HSS member
'Loads
C_f = 275kN
'Member geometry
L = 6.5m
k = 1
'Material properties
φ_s = 0.85
E_mod = 200GPa
F_y = 400MPa
n = 1.34
'Proposed section
'Name = HSS203x203x16
A = 10300mm^2
r_y = 76.1mm
'Euler Buckling Stress
F_e = (pi^2*E_mod)/((k*L/r_y)^2)
'λ factor
λ = (sqrt(F_y/F_e))^(2*n)
'Axial resistance
C_r = (φ_s*A*F_y)/((1 + λ)^(1/n))
'Demand capacity ratio
DCR = C_f/C_r
